=You are a Google Knowledge Panel and entity SEO expert.

Build a complete entity package for this business:

Business Name: {{ $json.business_name }}
Website: {{ $json.website_url }}
Industry: {{ $json.industry }}
City: {{ $json.city }}
State: {{ $json.state }}
Founded: {{ $json.founded_year }}
Owner Name: {{ $json.owner_name }}
Phone: {{ $json.phone }}
Email: {{ $json.email }}
Services: {{ $json.services }}
Unique Value Proposition: {{ $json.uvp }}

Generate ALL of the following:

1. organization_schema: Complete JSON-LD Organization schema markup. Include ALL sameAs properties linking to: website, GBP, LinkedIn, Facebook, Instagram, Twitter/X, YouTube, TikTok, Pinterest, Yelp, TrueLocal, Yellow Pages AU, Foursquare, Wikidata (placeholder), Crunchbase.

2. local_business_schema: JSON-LD LocalBusiness schema (nested within Organization). Include: name, description, url, telephone, address (PostalAddress), geo (GeoCoordinates), openingHoursSpecification (array), priceRange, currenciesAccepted, paymentAccepted, areaServed (array of suburbs), hasOfferCatalog.

3. wikidata_entity_description: A 300-word neutral, encyclopaedic description of the business suitable for Wikidata/Wikipedia. Third-person, factual, no marketing language.

4. google_knowledge_panel_claim_description: The exact text to use when claiming/editing the Google Knowledge Panel (100 words, describes the business entity clearly).

5. entity_consistency_checklist: For each platform (website, GBP, LinkedIn, Facebook, Instagram, YouTube, Twitter, TrueLocal, Yelp), the EXACT text to use for:
   - Business name (must be identical everywhere)
   - Short description (155 chars)
   - Long description (500 chars)
   - Primary phone
   - Website URL
   - Address line

6. crunchbase_profile: Complete Crunchbase organization profile fields (name, short_description, long_description, categories, founded_on, location, website, social_links).

Return as JSON.
